{
  "_comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the demo levels.",
    "Two tools read this file: tools/author-demo-scenes.py writes the committed .unity scenes,",
    "and Server/tools/GenerateSampleArtifact writes seed artifacts the web viewer can show",
    "before anyone opens Unity. The Unity bake of the scenes remains authoritative; the seed",
    "artifacts exist so the server demo works on a fresh checkout.",
    "Rotations are single-axis on purpose: one non-zero euler component converts to a quaternion",
    "the same way in every tool, so a scene and its seed artifact cannot drift over rotation order.",
    "Capsules are uniform-scaled: radius = 0.5 * scale, cylinder length = scale, total height = 2 * scale."
  ],
  "world": {
    "gravity": [0.0, -9.81, 0.0],
    "tickRate": 60,
    "substepCount": 1,
    "solverIterations": 6,
    "relaxationIterations": 4,
    "allowDeactivation": true
  },
